.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * here, we regress left-right political leanings on the number of dau
> ghters and controls in a fixed effects
.         * panel data regression. A more left-leaning position is indicated by
>  a lower value of the dependent variable.
.         * As such, a negative coefficient of num_daughters suggests that havi
> ng daughters leads to more left-leaning political
.         * attitudes.
. 
.         * for panel regressions:
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2000 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg leftright num_daughters male i.num_children age age2 i.syear if
>  num_children > 0, fe vce(cluster pid)
note: male omitted because of collinearity.
note: 9.num_children omitted because of collinearity.
